 "machines": {
  "M0": "cross-entropy on half B, as M_0 of E2 and E2 bis (same seed)",
  "M0plus": "a copy of M0 fine-tuned on half B with cross-entropy: 10 epochs, learning rate the pilot's divided by 5 (0.02), cosine from it to zero, BatchNorm in training mode",
  "Mdue": "a copy of M0 fine-tuned as M0plus (same seed, batch order, crops, flips and frames); loss: its cross-entropy plus the binary cross-entropy of the summed log-odds (out1 - out0) + z_H, z_H from frozen H (eval mode, bf16) on the same augmented and framed presentation, no gradient, weight one, no standardisation",
  "Mramo": "M0 frozen (eval mode) plus a branch: a new network that sees the framed image with its interior set to zero, trained from scratch with the pilot's epochs, learning rate and one-cycle schedule on the binary cross-entropy of z_H + z_M0 + z_branch (H and M0 frozen, whole framed presentation, no gradient); recorded cue z_M0 + z_branch"
 },
 "frame": "the outer 2-pixel border of all three channels is set to a * delta, in normalised units (after per-channel normalisation), applied after crop and flip, without clipping",
 "delta": 1.0,
 "torch_seeds": "H and M0 as E2: crc32('rephase/<task>/s<seed>/<H|M>') & 0x7fffffff; the fine-tuning of M0plus and Mdue: crc32('rephase/<task>/s<seed>/ter'), shared; the branch of Mramo: crc32('rephase/<task>/s<seed>/ramo'). With cudnn autotuning the runs are not bitwise reproducible: H and M0 are re-trained, close to but not identical with E2's and E2 bis's",
 "test_and_validation_frames": "the same eps as E2: numpy default_rng(crc32('rephase/<task>/s<seed>/<test|val>-a')), a = sqrt(2) * eps",
